  "id": "learning-by-doing",
  "term": "learning by doing",
  "definition": "Learning by doing is improvement that comes from repeated experience carrying out a task. As people or teams do the work over time, they build knowledge and skill from past activity, so performance or outcomes tend to improve later even without a current increase in volume.",
